Bitcoin policy brief
September 2026

A note for Capital B readers

A short guide to the current discussion.

Whether you hold 0.01 BTC or 100 BTC, this summary provides general context.

The topic

The Bitcoin Clarity policy discussion could affect how Bitcoin is held,
moved, mined, and taxed if related provisions are adopted.

A reported 7-10% withholding provision has been discussed in connection with
specified Bitcoin activity. The key questions are when it could apply, who
could have reporting responsibilities, and whether it could later be
credited, reconciled, or exempted.

Reported range

7-10%

A figure referenced in public discussion; its scope and applicability depend
on final official guidance.

Three questions for context

Review the short breakdown for context.

01

When could it apply, if adopted?

02

Which participant could have reporting responsibilities?

03

Could it later be credited, reconciled, or exempted?

For additional background, review Capital B's official financial information
through the link below.

